  "backtestId": "sha256:8796c929aec8874cf1be7f35cc9a60b67f210b24dce81a4337695fb6ea8d179d",
  "banner": "The planner's figures are a model, not a bound: this check measures how far off they are on this fleet.",
  "verdict": "Over the 1 h 13 min the planner did not see: mean TTFT: within 20% of measured in 6 of the 12 five-minute steps scored (a figure, and enough measured requests); it leans high (median ratio 1.21). For 1 more it gave no figure, calling the fleet overloaded; the fleet measured mean 11.6 s there. p90 TTFT: within 20% in 0 of 5, median ratio 1.35. p90 TTFT not scored in 2: the measured p90 fell in a histogram bucket wider than 20% of its lower edge, too wide to place it, with the prediction inside it or within 20% of its edge; in the measured histogram bucket itself in 1, 200 ms to 400 ms (2.0x wide): consistent at the bucket's resolution, not within 20%, and outside it, within 20% of its edge, in 1. mean TPOT: within 20% of measured in 13 of the 13 five-minute steps scored (a figure, and enough measured requests); no overall lean (median ratio 0.99). p90 TPOT not scored in 8: the measured p90 fell in a histogram bucket wider than 20% of its lower edge, too wide to place it, with the prediction inside it or within 20% of its edge; in the measured histogram bucket itself in 8, 10 ms to 20 ms (2.0x wide): consistent at the bucket's resolution, not within 20%. To measure it, give the histogram finer edges: the router's metrics.requestTPOTBuckets in the EndpointPickerConfig (an llm-d-router build after v1.0.0), or vLLM's --custom-histogram-buckets (v0.32.0 and later). Edges about 15% apart place p90 and p95 within 20%. None of these figures falls within the conditions our own accuracy benchmarks cover (docs/guides/capacity-planner/accuracy.md): this check is the evidence for this fleet.",
  "verdictLines": [
    "Over the 1 h 13 min the planner did not see:",
    "mean TTFT: within 20% of measured in 6 of the 12 five-minute steps scored (a figure, and enough measured requests); it leans high (median ratio 1.21). For 1 more it gave no figure, calling the fleet overloaded; the fleet measured mean 11.6 s there. p90 TTFT: within 20% in 0 of 5, median ratio 1.35. p90 TTFT not scored in 2: the measured p90 fell in a histogram bucket wider than 20% of its lower edge, too wide to place it, with the prediction inside it or within 20% of its edge; in the measured histogram bucket itself in 1, 200 ms to 400 ms (2.0x wide): consistent at the bucket's resolution, not within 20%, and outside it, within 20% of its edge, in 1.",
    "mean TPOT: within 20% of measured in 13 of the 13 five-minute steps scored (a figure, and enough measured requests); no overall lean (median ratio 0.99). p90 TPOT not scored in 8: the measured p90 fell in a histogram bucket wider than 20% of its lower edge, too wide to place it, with the prediction inside it or within 20% of its edge; in the measured histogram bucket itself in 8, 10 ms to 20 ms (2.0x wide): consistent at the bucket's resolution, not within 20%. To measure it, give the histogram finer edges: the router's metrics.requestTPOTBuckets in the EndpointPickerConfig (an llm-d-router build after v1.0.0), or vLLM's --custom-histogram-buckets (v0.32.0 and later). Edges about 15% apart place p90 and p95 within 20%.",
    "None of these figures falls within the conditions our own accuracy benchmarks cover (docs/guides/capacity-planner/accuracy.md): this check is the evidence for this fleet."
  ],
